│ ┃  Patch to Fix Inconsistent Type Alias Documentation in Sphinx  ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue arises from the fact that the autodoc extension in       │
│ Sphinx is not properly parsing the docstrings for type aliases in  │
│ the file.py module. This results in only some type aliases being   │
│ rendered, while others are ignored. The root cause is that the     │
│ autodoc extension is not enabled in the configuration file, or the │
│ toctree in index.rst is missing the file module.                   │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                          ✅ Patch Summary                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Enable the autodoc extension in conf.py to ensure proper        │
│    documentation parsing.                                          │
│  • Add the file module to the toctree in index.rst to ensure it    │
